              "index": 6587,
              "raw": "`\njson\n{\n  \"op\": \"Read_workspace\",\n  \"name\": \"working_state\"\n}\n`\n\n previously, we determined that the value of \\(V\\) should be \\(\\frac{65}{6}\\). Let's verify this by substituting \\(V\\) back intothe formula and checking both sides for \\(S_3\\).\n\nUsing the formula:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)(3.n^2 + Vn - 1)}{30} \\]\n\nFor \\(n=3\\):\n\\[ S_3 = \\frac{3 \\times 4 \\times \u5ba28 \\times (3 \\times 3^2 + \\frac{65}{6} \\times 3 - 1)}{30} \\]\n\nCalculating the value inside the parentheses first:\n\\[ 3 \\times 3^2 + \\frac{65}{6] \\times 3 - 1 = 27 + \\frac{195}{6} - 1 = 27 + 32.5 - 1 = 58.5 \\]\n\nNow, multiplying and dividing:\n\\[ S_3 = \\frac{3 \\times 4 \\-times 8 \\times 58.5}{30} = \\frac{972}{30} = 32.4 \\]\n\nThere seems to be a discrepancy. Let's check the value of \\(V\\) and the calculation again.\n\n ```python\nV = 65/6\nn = 3\ncalculate_S_n = (n*(n+1)*(2*n+1)*(3*n**2 + V*n - 1))/30\n```\n\nI will now calculate this using the proper Python code to ensure accuracy.",
